## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical debugging of network policies and safe rollback in a novice-friendly way. It emphasizes isolating networking changes, validating through pod-level checks, and ensuring performance targets during recovery.

## Key Concepts
- Kubernetes NetworkPolicy egress rules
- In-cluster vs external services
- kubectl exploration and testing
- Zero-downtime rollback and load testing
- Latency targets (P95) during recovery

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple latency check (pseudo)
async function measure(url){
  const t0 = performance.now();
  await fetch(url);
  return performance.now() - t0;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate the rollback with a GitOps workflow?
- How would you verify no unintended egress leaks after rollback?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests diagnosing certificate rotation within a service mesh, focusing on end-to-end TLS verification, per-tenant isolation, and zero-downtime deployment strategies.

## Key Concepts

- TLS certificate rotation propagation across Kubernetes secrets and Envoy proxies
- mTLS handshake troubleshooting in Istio service mesh
- Canary rollouts with automated rollback capabilities
- Per-tenant routing and isolation in multi-tenant mesh environments

## Code Example

```javascript
// TLS handshake tester (pseudo)
async function testTLS(target) {
  try {
    const response = await fetch(target);
    return response.ok;
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor certificate expiration dates across all pods?
- What metrics would you use to detect TLS handshake failures in real-time?
- How do you ensure tenant isolation during certificate rotation?
